# Batch 6 prompts (30 gods x 2 styles x 4 actions). Writes b3/p6.json {clip: prompt}.
# Rules applied (KLING_RULES.md): tight canvas, fixed camera, idle moves clearly but calmly, never a turntable;
# weapons never at full arm's length / never aimed sideways; ranged = up or toward the viewer, game continues it;
# melee = strike close in front of the body (the game leaps to the enemy); buffs/heals rise from the hand straight up
# (the game flies them to the allies); no white-out/flare/star glint/rings/threads from edges; same richness both styles.
import json

CAM = "Fixed camera, the flat gray background stays exactly the same, no camera movement, no zoom. "
END_ACT = (" Rich, clearly visible {col}, medium brightness, in both the effect and the glow on the body. All moves are smooth "
           "and continuous, no sudden jumps, no flicker. No white-out, no lens flare, no starburst, no star-shaped or "
           "cross-shaped glint, no full-frame flash, the background never brightens; no glow and no rings on the ground; no "
           "threads or lines of light in the air, nothing flies in from the edges; nothing is aimed or thrown to the left or "
           "to the right; effects stay close to the body and do not touch the left and right edges of the frame. "
           "{noextra}The end pose equals the start pose.")
IDLE = ("Idle loop with clear continuous motion the whole time, {he} is never still: {he} slowly sways {his} torso and "
        "shoulders, shifts {his} weight from one leg to the other, takes a slow small step to the side with one foot and a "
        "slow step back, bends and straightens {his} knees a little, turns {his} head to the left and then to the right, "
        "breathes so {his} chest rises and falls; {extra}. {keep} {His} hips and chest always face the viewer: the body "
        "never turns or spins like a figurine on a stand, any shift happens through the feet stepping. All moves are slow "
        "and smooth, no dancing, no fast or sharp gestures. No other magic effects. The end pose equals the start pose.")

